'''Pokémon Hills''' (Japanese: '''ポケモンヒルズ''' ''Pokémon Hills'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive location in [[Unova]], and one of the settings of ''[[M16|Genesect and the Legend Awakened]]''. It is a park located at the center of [[New Tork City]] specially constructed for the housing of {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}.

Pokémon Hills has a number of different environments that are suitable for the many kinds of Pokémon living there. It also has a hedge maze. According to [[Eric]], the area surrounding Pokémon Hills has plants from all over the {{pkmn|world}}.

During the {{pkmn|movie}}, the [[Genesect Army]] invaded Pokémon Hills thinking the park was their home and forced all the Pokémon to leave so that they could build a giant nest. Later, the Pokémon from Pokémon Hills returned and had a big fight with the Genesect Army. The battle ended after {{OBP|Mewtwo|M16}} took the {{pkmn2|Shiny}} {{p|Genesect}} to the atmosphere and explained that [[human]]s and Pokémon live together in the Pokémon world and are friends with them. After that, {{Ash}} found the perfect place for the Genesect Army to live in [[Absentia Natural Park]], where Panna Lotuses—flowers that have been around since the Genesect were last alive—bloom in abundance.

